<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto II, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1206–1253</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Otto the Illustrious</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto II, called the Illustrious, was a Wittelsbach Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 1231 to 1253 and, through his marriage to Agnes of the Palatinate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> from 1228. He supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> emperors against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> and was excommunicated. On his death his sons Louis II and Henry XIII divided the duchy in 1255, the first of many Wittelsbach partitions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-ii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Otto II, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_II_Wittelsbach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
